From 52a478a1fa9e60d8d97d67d68575b722e3120d59 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 22:06:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dialogs: the player information of Hades as a dialog of its
 own, for any skin

A skin other than Estuary has its own player process information, without
the overview and Dolby Vision pages of Hades. They are now a dialog of
their own, "hadesplayerinfo" (CGUIDialogHadesPlayerInfo, window 10199, an
id Kodi does not use): the skin's DialogHadesPlayerInfo.xml if it has one,
else system/hades/DialogHadesPlayerInfo.xml in Estuary's coordinates, as a
script window falls back to its own skin folder. That one is Estuary's two
pages, made from Estuary's file (tools/hades-playerinfo/make-playerinfo.py)
with the includes expanded and Estuary's control defaults written into each
control, so that the look does not come from the other skin's defaults; its
variables are those every skin is given (the commit before). Kodi's font
names that a skin does not have fall back to font13.

It opens with ActivateWindow(hadesplayerinfo) and, for a video, with a
second press of the key that opens the player process information, where
the skin's dialog does not show these pages itself (it reads no
Window(Home).Property(hades.*)): in Estuary nothing changes. The same key
closes it (keyboard o, the remote's title, the gamepad's black, as for the
player process information). The window system publishes the properties of
the overview page while it is shown, as it does for the player process
information.

Compiled with Kodi's compile commands (-fsyntax-only): the new dialog, the
player process information, the window manager, the window translator,
CSkinInfo and the window system. The keymaps parse. Not run in Kodi (no GUI
in the tests here): not seen with any skin.
